# Line endings are content here, not preference.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) writes CRLF into
# every text file, and `gofmt` treats a CRLF file as unformatted — so
# `make lint` reported the entire Go module as broken on Windows while the
# committed bytes were clean. The same class of bug hits shell scripts (a CRLF
# `#!/bin/sh` fails to execute inside a container) and SQL applied by goose.
#
# Everything text-like is normalised to LF in the working tree, on every OS.
# The two Windows entry points keep CRLF, because that is what cmd.exe and
# PowerShell expect from a file they execute.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
